               <provenance>According to Additio 2, the Ms. was purchased
                     by priest (qasis ) Walda Mikāʾel. His name and that of his wife Walatta Śǝllāse
                     have been written (later?) throughout the Ms. by a secondary hand, in moderate
                     crimson (18ra, 21ra, 32ra, 78va, 102rb, 114vb,
                     117vb, 123vb, 131ra).</provenance></history>
